{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n\n    private static class PowerInfo {\n        int cur;\n        double value;\n\n        PowerInfo(int cur, double value) {\n            this.cur = cur;\n            this.value = value;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public void solve() {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long W = sc.nextLong();\n        long M = sc.nextLong();\n\n        PowerInfo info = ceilPower(W, M);\n        double pw = info.value;\n\n        if (pw == M) {\n            System.out.println(\"YES\");\n            return;\n        }\n\n        long max = (long) pw;\n        long sum = (max - 1) / (W - 1);\n        if (max - sum == M) {\n            System.out.println(\"YES\");\n            return;\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(dfs(W, M) ? \"YES\" : \"NO\");\n    }\n\n    private PowerInfo ceilPower(long W, long M) {\n        int cur = 0;\n        while (Math.pow(W, cur) < M) {\n            cur++;\n        }\n        return new PowerInfo(cur, Math.pow(W, cur));\n    }\n\n    private boolean dfs(long W, long M) {\n        if (M == 1) {\n            return true;\n        }\n        if (M % W == 0) {\n            return dfs(W, M / W);\n        } else if ((M - 1) % W == 0) {\n            return dfs(W, (M - 1) / W);\n        } else if ((M + 1) % W == 0) {\n            return dfs(W, (M + 1) / W);\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        new Main().solve();\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cmath>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nstruct PowerInfo {\n    int cur;\n    double value;\n    PowerInfo(int c, double v) : cur(c), value(v) {}\n};\n\nPowerInfo ceilPower(long long W, long long M) {\n    int cur = 0;\n    while (pow(W, cur) < M) {\n        cur++;\n    }\n    return PowerInfo(cur, pow(W, cur));\n}\n\nbool dfs(long long W, long long M) {\n    if (M == 1) return true;\n    if (M % W == 0) return dfs(W, M / W);\n    else if ((M - 1) % W == 0) return dfs(W, (M - 1) / W);\n    else if ((M + 1) % W == 0) return dfs(W, (M + 1) / W);\n    return false;\n}\n\nvoid solve() {\n    long long W, M;\n    cin >> W >> M;\n\n    PowerInfo info = ceilPower(W, M);\n    double pw = info.value;\n\n    if (pw == M) {\n        cout << \"YES\" << endl;\n        return;\n    }\n\n    long long max = (long long)pw;\n    long long sum = (max - 1) / (W - 1);\n    if (max - sum == M) {\n        cout << \"YES\" << endl;\n        return;\n    }\n\n    cout << (dfs(W, M) ? \"YES\" : \"NO\") << endl;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    solve();\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00020752183627337217, -1.9430925021879375e-05, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -5.960446742392378e-06, -1.6689160474925302e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.4741019010543823, -0.01819409430027008, -9.619726915843785e-05, 0.0, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.0003961731